. If\n169:### 2.4 `meta.json`\n262:| `captured` | bool, always |\n304:`caveats`: human strings from snapshot capture (snapshot area).\n308:1. Validate `meta.run_id` (error `write meta: invalid run id \"<id>\"`).\n319:Resolve `runDir(id)` (2.10). Read `meta.json` (error\n325:### 2.5 `env_names_only` (`captureEnv`)\n340:- Validate `runID` (error `write artifact: invalid run id \"<id>\"`) and\n358:`write <path>: <err>`); empty run ID -> `write report: empty run id`.\n360:### 2.7 `provider-responses.jsonl`\n390:- Invalid or empty run ID -> `record provider response: invalid run id`.\n396:`close <path>: ...`); the llm area decides what a capture failure does to\n401:The 16 MiB cap on a captured body is enforced by the llm area before\n404:### 2.8 `findings.jsonl` (finding spill)\n407:directory is `\"\"`, the run ID is empty, or `makeRunDir` fails (checked\n427:File: `<recordsDir>/runs-<YYYY>-<MM>.jsonl`, year and month in the\n429:appended after the bundle is built.\n485:   `.jsonl`. Sort full paths descending (bytewise) and keep the first\n508:1. `id` must be a valid name (2.2), else `invalid run id \"<id>\"`.\n519:`reportPath(id)` = `<runDir(id)>/report.md`. A full run ID or any unique\n542:  - `meta.ts`, `findings.jsonl` `ts`: UTC, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS[.frac]Z`,\n552:### 2.12 Run bundle (`bundle.tar.zst`)\n556:- `BundleFile = \"bundle.tar.zst\"`\n557:- `ManifestFile = \"bundle-manifest.json\"` (only inside the archive, never\n// A `node:http` fake inference server (Go httptest plus providerServer):\n// it records every request and answers from a script that looks at the\n// request (path, body, headers) and the request's position.\nimport {\n    createServer,\n    type IncomingHttpHeaders,\n    type ServerResponse,\n} from 'node:http'\nimport type { AddressInfo } from 'node:net'\nimport { writeInferenceStream } from './inference-stream.js'\n\nexport interface RecordedRequest {\n    method:string;\n    path:string;\n    headers:IncomingHttpHeaders;\n    // Header names