{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChB45FwyoXGbCNtuCaKNL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] The CI differential job runs on Ubuntu and fails on a non-allowlisted difference.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass; `go test ./...` still passes.\n\nThe differential harness is built and committed, and all 50 M1 scenarios pass against the real Go baseline built from `cd08f10`. `npm run lint`, `typecheck`, `test:ts` (3122 tests), `npm test` (which includes `go test ./...`) and `npm run test:diff` all pass. The one thing not yet seen is the new CI job running on GitHub. It passes `actionlint`, and a local run exited 1 on a real difference before I added it to the allowlist, so the job should fail the same way.\n\n**How it runs.** `npm run test:diff` bundles the CLI and `test/diff/index.ts`, then runs everything in one TAP stream:\n1. Self-tests of the harness itself, which need no Go.\n2. Every scenario, each run as two processes: the Go baseline binary and `node dist/cli.js`.\n\nEach CLI gets its own fixture repository with fixed identity and dates, so commit IDs match, and a scrubbed environment with a private `HOME`. Without `go` on `PATH`, all 50 scenarios print as TAP skips and the run exits 0.\n\n**Where things are:**\n- **Baseline build** (`test/diff/baseline.ts`): uses a temporary worktree and caches the binary at `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/roast-go-cd08f10`.\n- **Comparison layer**, ready for the later review scenarios: normalization of run IDs, timestamps, durations, paths, build identity and session IDs; run-record comparison (bundles read as decompressed tar entries); request comparison grouped by model and turn count; and the allowlist.\n- **M1 scenarios** (`test/diff/scenarios/m1.ts`): 8 valid and 17 invalid config cases, each run through both `gate settings` and `trust --yes`.\n- **CI**: a new Ubuntu job, `differential`, in `ci.yml` (Node 22, full history so `cd08f10` is there).\n\n**Checks against the acceptance criteria:**\n- A second run with a logging `go` wrapper on `PATH` never called `go`.\n- Self-tests with a fake `go` confirm the worktree is removed after both a successful and a failing build.\n- A stub CLI that exits 3, and one that prints a different severity, are both reported as unexplained differences.\n- A stub that writes a fresh run ID, timestamp, version, session ID and repository path each run compares equal across two runs.\n- Breaking any one normalization rule in the built bundle makes the self-tests fail.\n\n**Decisions to review:**\n- **One difference is allowlisted.** Go accepts the key `\"Gate\"` case-insensitively and exits 0; the TS CLI rejects it and exits 2. That is deliberate change 7 (exact-case JSON keys), and the allowlist entry is limited to that one scenario.\n- **No `go` means skip, even with a cached binary.** I check for `go` before looking at the cache, so every scenario still skips as the acceptance criterion requires. The spec's step order (reuse the cache first) could be read the other way.\n\nI also added a short section on the harness to `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":164341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c00c7f3-71f4-4751-b678-7052dcc92742","uuid":"22cbe832-0cec-4d93-a59c-a88b49d0391f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:50:47.121Z","request_id":"req_011ChB45FaAEM8X264yfZpGg"}
